---
const { kind } = Astro.props;
const cases = [
  ['number', 'JSON number · 300'], ['string', 'JSON string · "300"'],
  ['null', 'JSON null'], ['missing', 'Field absent'], ['sqlnull', 'SQL NULL document'],
  ['zero', 'JSON number · 0'], ['word', 'JSON string · "large"'],
];
---
{kind === 'boundary' && <figure class="jf" aria-labelledby="jf-boundary-title">
  <figcaption id="jf-boundary-title"><span>Figure 1</span> One product, different kinds of fact</figcaption>
  <div class="jf-scene jf-boundary">
    <div class="jf-box"><strong>products · shared identity</strong><dl><dt>P3</dt><dd>Green tea, 50 g · 4.50</dd><dt>P7</dt><dd>Blue mug · 20.00</dd></dl><p>Price and stock keep their existing types and rules.</p></div>
    <div class="jf-arrow">↓ same product_id · choose a home for specialised details</div>
    <div class="jf-columns">
      <div class="jf-box"><strong>Typed detail rows</strong><dl><dt>tea_details · P3</dt><dd>origin text: Japan</dd><dt>teaware_details · P7</dt><dd>capacity_ml numeric: 300</dd></dl></div>
      <div class="jf-box"><strong>JSONB detail rows</strong><dl><dt>product_documents · P3</dt><dd><code>{'{"origin":"Japan"}'}</code></dd><dt>product_documents · P7</dt><dd><code>{'{"capacity_ml":300}'}</code></dd></dl></div>
    </div>
    <p class="jf-band">Alternative homes for the same specialised facts. Both keep a reference to products.</p>
    <div class="jf-box"><strong>Independent memberships · product_tags</strong><div class="jf-memberships"><span>P7 → gift</span><span>P7 → ceramic</span></div><p>Each pair has its own row. A tag can be added or referenced without replacing P7’s detail document.</p></div>
  </div>
  <p class="jf-caption">P3’s origin and P7’s capacity are the collection’s subtype example. The two middle panels are alternative representations, not two authorities to maintain together. Stock, orders and payments are unchanged.</p>
</figure>}
{kind === 'extract' && <figure class="jf jf-extract" aria-labelledby="jf-extract-title">
  <figcaption id="jf-extract-title"><span>Figure 2</span> One field through extraction and validation</figcaption>
  <div class="jf-scene">
    <label class="jf-option">Input <select data-case>{cases.map(([value,label]) => <option value={value}>{label}</option>)}</select></label>
    <div class="jf-box"><strong>details · stored JSONB</strong><pre data-document data-live>{'{"capacity_ml":300}'}</pre></div>
    <div class="jf-arrow">↓ extract capacity_ml</div>
    <div class="jf-columns">
      <div class="jf-box" data-stage="1"><strong><code>details -&gt; 'capacity_ml'</code></strong><p>Result type: jsonb</p><pre data-json data-live>—</pre><p data-json-type data-live>Not extracted yet.</p></div>
      <div class="jf-box" data-stage="1"><strong><code>details -&gt;&gt; 'capacity_ml'</code></strong><p>Result type: text</p><pre data-text data-live>—</pre><p>Text extraction removes the JSON type.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="jf-arrow">↓ required positive JSON number</div>
    <div class="jf-box jf-contract" data-stage="2"><strong>Object → present → number → positive</strong><p data-verdict data-live>Not tested yet.</p></div>
    <p data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">Start with the stored document. Its JSON number 300 has not been converted to text.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="jf-controls" role="group" aria-label="Figure 2 controls"><button data-play>Play</button><button data-back>Back</button><button data-next>Next</button><button data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 3</span><div data-hold><span></span></div></div>
  <p class="jf-caption">The stages explain the expressions and the contract below; they do not describe PostgreSQL’s physical execution order. Change the input, then step through it. Only the numeric 300 passes this required-positive-number contract.</p>
  <details><summary>All inputs and results, as text</summary><ul><li>Numeric 300: JSON extraction is 300, text extraction is 300; passes.</li><li>String “300”: JSON extraction is “300”, text extraction is 300; fails the JSON-number rule.</li><li>JSON null: JSON extraction is null, text extraction is SQL NULL; fails.</li><li>Absent field: both extractions are SQL NULL; fails.</li><li>SQL NULL document: both extractions are SQL NULL; fails NOT NULL.</li><li>Numeric zero: both extractions show 0; fails positivity.</li><li>String “large”: JSON extraction is “large”, text extraction is large; fails without attempting a numeric cast.</li></ul></details>
</figure>}
{kind === 'predicates' && <figure class="jf jf-predicates" aria-labelledby="jf-predicates-title">
  <figcaption id="jf-predicates-title"><span>Figure 3</span> A key, a contained fragment or the whole value</figcaption>
  <div class="jf-scene">
    <label class="jf-option">Question <select data-question><option value="exist">Top-level gift key</option><option value="element">Gift inside tags</option><option value="contain">Contains both tags</option><option value="equal">Equals the whole document</option></select></label>
    <pre data-predicate data-live>doc ? 'gift'</pre>
    <div class="jf-probe"><strong>P7 projection</strong><code>{'{"tags":["gift","ceramic"]}'}</code><span data-result="0" data-live>no</span></div>
    <div class="jf-probe"><strong>Reversed</strong><code>{'{"tags":["ceramic","gift"]}'}</code><span data-result="1" data-live>no</span></div>
    <div class="jf-probe"><strong>Extra</strong><code>{'{"tags":["gift","ceramic","sale"]}'}</code><span data-result="2" data-live>no</span></div>
    <div class="jf-probe"><strong>Repeated</strong><code>{'{"tags":["gift","ceramic","gift"]}'}</code><span data-result="3" data-live>no</span></div>
    <p class="jf-band" data-meaning data-live>The string gift is inside tags. It is not a top-level key of any document.</p>
  </div>
  <p class="jf-caption">P7’s established memberships supply the first diagnostic document. The other documents vary that value in an isolated test table, tag_probe; they are not extra products or new memberships. Containment ignores array order and repeated occurrences; whole-value equality preserves both.</p>
  <details><summary>All questions and answers, as text</summary><p>No document has a top-level gift key. Every tags array has gift, and every document contains the requested gift/ceramic fragment. Only the first equals the complete two-tag document.</p></details>
</figure>}
{kind === 'indexes' && <figure class="jf" aria-labelledby="jf-index-title">
  <figcaption id="jf-index-title"><span>Figure 4</span> The operator must reach the indexed expression</figcaption>
  <div class="jf-scene jf-index-map">
    <div class="jf-box"><strong>Match a document fragment</strong><code>doc @&gt; '{'{"tags":["gift"]}'}'::jsonb</code><div class="jf-arrow">↓ JSONB containment</div><p>GIN on <code>doc</code><br />jsonb_ops or jsonb_path_ops</p></div>
    <div class="jf-box"><strong>Membership inside tags</strong><code>(doc -&gt; 'tags') ? 'gift'</code><div class="jf-arrow">↓ existence on this subvalue</div><p>GIN on <code>(doc -&gt; 'tags')</code><br />jsonb_ops</p></div>
    <div class="jf-box"><strong>Capacity at least 300 ml, in order</strong><code>(details -&gt;&gt; 'capacity_ml')::numeric &gt;= 300</code><div class="jf-arrow">↓ numeric range and order</div><p>B-tree on that numeric expression<br />after validation</p></div>
  </div>
  <p class="jf-caption">Three possible access paths, not measured plans. Containment preserves the fragment’s nesting. The first two searches agree on these diagnostic tag arrays but apply their operators to different expressions. The third asks for a scalar range; a whole-document GIN does not supply that numeric order.</p>
</figure>}
{kind === 'writes' && <figure class="jf" aria-labelledby="jf-write-title">
  <figcaption id="jf-write-title"><span>Figure 5</span> Which value does the second edit start from?</figcaption>
  <div class="jf-scene">
    <div class="jf-box"><strong>Independent replay · both clients read P7</strong><code>{'{"capacity_ml":300}'}</code></div>
    <div class="jf-arrow">↓ A adds a local illustrative care instruction and commits</div>
    <div class="jf-box"><code>{'{"capacity_ml":300,"care":"hand wash"}'}</code></div>
    <div class="jf-columns">
      <div class="jf-box"><strong>B sends its old document, edited</strong><p>Replace details with:</p><code>{'{"capacity_ml":330}'}</code><p><strong>Care instruction lost.</strong><br />B’s replacement never contained it.</p></div>
      <div class="jf-box"><strong>B edits the stored value</strong><p><code>jsonb_set(details, …)</code></p><code>{'{"capacity_ml":330,"care":"hand wash"}'}</code><p><strong>Care instruction retained.</strong><br />B changes the capacity member.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="jf-caption">A conceptual Read Committed schedule: A has committed before B’s UPDATE starts. The alternatives start from the same state and do not both run. Capacity 330 and the care instruction are local diagnostic edits, not changes to the collection’s starting facts.</p>
</figure>}
<style>
  .jf { margin:2.4rem 0; font:.88rem/1.6 var(--font-sans); }
  .jf figcaption { margin-bottom:.65rem; font:1.12rem/1.5 var(--font-serif); }
  .jf figcaption > span { margin-right:.7rem; font:.65rem/1.5 var(--font-sans); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.1em; color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .jf-scene { padding:1rem; border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); background:var(--color-surface-alt); }
  .jf p { margin:.6rem 0; font:inherit; }
  .jf pre { margin:.4rem 0; white-space:pre-wrap; overflow-wrap:anywhere; padding:0; border:0; background:none; color:var(--color-text); font:.84rem/1.6 var(--font-mono); }
  .jf code { overflow-wrap:anywhere; font:.8rem/1.7 var(--font-mono); }
  .jf-box { padding:.8rem; border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); min-width:0; background:var(--color-surface); }
  .jf-box > strong { display:block; margin-bottom:.5rem; }
  .jf-columns { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:.7rem; }
  .jf-arrow { padding:.6rem .2rem; color:var(--color-text-secondary); text-align:center; }
  .jf-band { border-left:3px solid var(--color-text-secondary); padding:.55rem .8rem; }
  .jf dl { margin:0; }.jf dt { font-weight:600; margin-top:.5rem; }.jf dd { margin:.1rem 0; }
  .jf-memberships { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:.5rem; }.jf-memberships span { padding:.3rem .6rem; border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); }
  .jf .jf-caption { margin-top:.7rem; color:var(--color-text-secondary); font:.8rem/1.65 var(--font-sans); }
  .jf-option { display:block; margin-bottom:1rem; font-weight:600; }.jf select { display:block; max-width:100%; width:100%; margin-top:.4rem; font:inherit; padding:.5rem; background:var(--color-surface); color:var(--color-text); border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .jf-controls { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; align-items:center; gap:.5rem; padding:.8rem; border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); border-top:0; background:var(--color-surface-alt); }
  .jf button { padding:.4rem .65rem; font:inherit; color:var(--color-text); background:var(--color-surface); border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary); cursor:pointer; }
  .jf button[aria-disabled="true"] { color:var(--color-text-secondary); border-style:dashed; cursor:default; }
  .jf button:focus-visible,.jf select:focus-visible,.jf summary:focus-visible { outline:2px solid var(--color-text); outline-offset:3px; }
  .jf [data-hold] { flex-basis:100%; height:2px; background:var(--color-rule); }.jf [data-hold] span { display:block; height:2px; width:0; background:var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .jf [data-explanation] { padding:.65rem 0 0; min-height:5rem; }
  .jf [data-stage][data-pending] { border-style:dashed; }
  .jf-probe { display:grid; grid-template-columns:6.7rem 1fr 2rem; gap:.5rem; padding:.7rem 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); align-items:center; }
  .jf-probe span { font-weight:700; }.jf-index-map { display:grid; gap:.7rem; }
  .jf details { margin-top:.8rem; }.jf summary { cursor:pointer; color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
  @media(max-width:550px) { .jf-scene{padding:.65rem}.jf-columns{grid-template-columns:1fr}.jf-extract .jf-columns{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.jf-extract .jf-columns .jf-box{padding:.55rem}.jf-probe{grid-template-columns:1fr 2rem}.jf-probe code{grid-column:1;grid-row:auto}.jf-probe span{grid-column:2;grid-row:span 2}.jf [data-explanation]{min-height:5rem}.jf-box{padding:.65rem} }
</style>
<script>
  import { stepper } from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
  const inputs = {
    number: {doc:'{"capacity_ml":300}', json:'300', type:'number', text:'300', verdict:'Pass: present JSON number 300 is greater than zero.', reason:'Both outputs display 300. Only JSON extraction still says it is a number.'},
    string: {doc:'{"capacity_ml":"300"}', json:'"300"', type:'string', text:'300', verdict:'Reject: this is a JSON string, even though its text can be cast to numeric.', reason:'Text extraction looks the same as for numeric 300. JSON extraction retains the string distinction.'},
    null: {doc:'{"capacity_ml":null}', json:'null', type:'null', text:'SQL NULL', verdict:'Reject: the field exists, but JSON null is not a number.', reason:'JSON extraction preserves JSON null. Text extraction returns SQL NULL.'},
    missing: {doc:'{}', json:'SQL NULL', type:'SQL NULL', text:'SQL NULL', verdict:'Reject: the required member is absent.', reason:'Both extractions return SQL NULL. Neither invents a capacity for a missing member.'},
    sqlnull: {doc:'SQL NULL', json:'SQL NULL', type:'SQL NULL', text:'SQL NULL', verdict:'Reject: NOT NULL forbids an absent document.', reason:'There is no document from which to extract a member. Both results are SQL NULL.'},
    zero: {doc:'{"capacity_ml":0}', json:'0', type:'number', text:'0', verdict:'Reject: the JSON number is not positive.', reason:'The JSON type is right. Its value still has to satisfy the positive-capacity rule.'},
    word: {doc:'{"capacity_ml":"large"}', json:'"large"', type:'string', text:'large', verdict:'Reject: the JSON type is wrong. No numeric cast is attempted.', reason:'A direct numeric cast of large would fail. The guarded contract rejects its type first.'},
  };
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.jf-extract').forEach(root => {
    const choose = root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-case]')!;
    const set = (selector:string, text:string) => { root.querySelector(selector)!.textContent=text; };
    const player = stepper(root, {steps:()=>3, draw:(step:number)=> {
      const item=inputs[choose.value as keyof typeof inputs];
      set('[data-document]',item.doc);
      set('[data-json]',step>0?item.json:'—');
      set('[data-text]',step>0?item.text:'—');
      set('[data-json-type]',step>0?`jsonb_typeof of the result: ${item.type}`:'Not extracted yet.');
      set('[data-verdict]',step>1?item.verdict:'Not tested yet.');
      set('[data-explanation]',step===0?'Start with the stored input. Its JSON shape and types have not been erased by text extraction.':step===1?item.reason:item.verdict+' The SQL contract uses CASE to guard conversion.');
      root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-stage]').forEach(node=>node.toggleAttribute('data-pending',step<Number(node.dataset.stage)));
    }});
    choose.addEventListener('change',()=>player.render());
  });
  const questions = {
    exist: {sql:"doc ? 'gift'", answers:[false,false,false,false], text:'The string gift is inside tags. It is not a top-level key of any document.'},
    element: {sql:"(doc -> 'tags') ? 'gift'", answers:[true,true,true,true], text:'The left operand is now the tags array. Every array has the string gift.'},
    contain: {sql:`doc @> '{"tags":["gift","ceramic"]}'::jsonb`,answers:[true,true,true,true],text:'The fragment fits inside every document. Extra elements, reversed order and repetition do not defeat containment.'},
    equal: {sql:`doc = '{"tags":["gift","ceramic"]}'::jsonb`,answers:[true,false,false,false],text:'Whole-value equality requires the same array sequence, including its length and repeated elements. Only the first document matches.'},
  };
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.jf-predicates').forEach(root=> {
    const choose=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-question]')!;
    const draw=()=>{const item=questions[choose.value as keyof typeof questions];root.querySelector('[data-predicate]')!.textContent=item.sql;root.querySelector('[data-meaning]')!.textContent=item.text;root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-result]').forEach((node,i)=>node.textContent=item.answers[i]?'yes':'no');};
    choose.addEventListener('change',draw);draw();
  });
</script>
